    "summary": "Alligator→Eleven jam shines; Easy Wind lifts second set",
    "blurb": "Highlights include a smoking Alligator → Drums → The Eleven sequence and an outstanding Easy Wind. The band delivers tight early‑70 set work with a fiery China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider transition, despite a few tape cuts of Cumberland Blues.",
    "review": "Portland’s Springer's Inn on Jan 16, 1970 captured the Dead in a classic early‑70 groove. The first set kicks off with a tight run through Casey Jones and Mama Tried before launching into a smoking Alligator → Drums → The Eleven jam that showcases Jerry’s crisp tone and the dual drummers’ kinetic energy. A concise Death Don't Have No Mercy rounds out the first half, while the second set lifts off with a blistering China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider and rolls into solid renditions of Dire Wolf, Uncle John’s Band (complete with a witty intro from Phil) and an uplifting Easy Wind that carries the show to its climactic The Other One/cryptical envelopment finale. Though the early tape suffers a couple of cuts on Cumberland Blues, the overall soundboard capture is clear, balanced, and lets the band’s tight interplay shine.",
